{
  "id": "m04-inversion-count",
  "title": "Count the Inversions",
  "source": {
    "name": "Original exercise on divide and conquer recurrences (merge sort)"
  },
  "rating": 1600,
  "tags": [
    "divide-and-conquer",
    "merge-sort",
    "recurrence"
  ],
  "statement": "An inversion is a pair of indices `i < j` with `a_i > a_j`. Count the inversions in a given sequence of `n` integers.\n\n**Input.** First line: `n`. Second line: the `n` integers.\n\n**Output.** The number of inversions.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 2000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "0 ≤ a_i ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Checking all pairs is O(n^2): 4.5 million pairs here, but 2 * 10^10 at n = 2 * 10^5. Look for a divide-and-conquer structure.",
    "Split the array in halves. Inversions are within the left half, within the right half, or across. Recurse for the first two.",
    "Sort while counting. When merging two sorted halves, every time you take an element from the right half, it forms an inversion with all remaining elements of the left half. That is T(n) = 2T(n/2) + O(n) = O(n log n). Use a 64-bit counter."
  ],
  "editorial": "Merge sort with a counter. After recursively sorting and counting both halves, merge them. While merging, if the next element comes from the right half (strictly smaller than the current left element), it is smaller than all `mid - i` remaining left elements, so add `mid - i` to the count. Equal elements are not inversions, so take from the left on ties.\n\nThe recurrence `T(n) = 2T(n/2) + Theta(n)` solves to `Theta(n log n)` by the master theorem (case 2). The count can reach `n(n-1)/2`, about `2 * 10^10` at `n = 2 * 10^5`, so a 64-bit counter is required at full scale.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\n# count pairs i<j with a[i] > a[j] in O(n log n)\n",
    "javascript": "const n = Number(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    // merge sort and count\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        // merge sort and count\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\n\ndef sort_count(arr):\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return arr, 0\n    mid = len(arr) // 2\n    left, cl = sort_count(arr[:mid])\n    right, cr = sort_count(arr[mid:])\n    merged = []\n    i = j = 0\n    cross = 0\n    while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n        if left[i] <= right[j]:\n            merged.append(left[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(right[j])\n            j += 1\n            cross += len(left) - i\n    merged.extend(left[i:])\n    merged.extend(right[j:])\n    return merged, cl + cr + cross\n\nprint(sort_count(a)[1])\n",
    "javascript": "const n = Number(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nfunction sortCount(arr) {\n  if (arr.length <= 1) return [arr, 0];\n  const mid = arr.length >> 1;\n  const [left, cl] = sortCount(arr.slice(0, mid));\n  const [right, cr] = sortCount(arr.slice(mid));\n  const merged = [];\n  let i = 0, j = 0, cross = 0;\n  while (i < left.length && j < right.length) {\n    if (left[i] <= right[j]) merged.push(left[i++]);\n    else { merged.push(right[j++]); cross += left.length - i; }\n  }\n  while (i < left.length) merged.push(left[i++]);\n  while (j < right.length) merged.push(right[j++]);\n  return [merged, cl + cr + cross];\n}\nconsole.log(String(sortCount(a)[1]));\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nlong long sortCount(vector<long long>& a, vector<long long>& tmp, int lo, int hi) {\n    if (hi - lo <= 1) return 0;\n    int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n    long long c = sortCount(a, tmp, lo, mid) + sortCount(a, tmp, mid, hi);\n    int i = lo, j = mid, k = lo;\n    while (i < mid && j < hi) {\n        if (a[i] <= a[j]) tmp[k++] = a[i++];\n        else { tmp[k++] = a[j++]; c += mid - i; }\n    }\n    while (i < mid) tmp[k++] = a[i++];\n    while (j < hi) tmp[k++] = a[j++];\n    for (int x = lo; x < hi; x++) a[x] = tmp[x];\n    return c;\n}\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n), tmp(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    cout << sortCount(a, tmp, 0, n) << endl;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long sortCount(long[] a, long[] tmp, int lo, int hi) {\n        if (hi - lo <= 1) return 0;\n        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        long c = sortCount(a, tmp, lo, mid) + sortCount(a, tmp, mid, hi);\n        int i = lo, j = mid, k = lo;\n        while (i < mid && j < hi) {\n            if (a[i] <= a[j]) tmp[k++] = a[i++];\n            else { tmp[k++] = a[j++]; c += mid - i; }\n        }\n        while (i < mid) tmp[k++] = a[i++];\n        while (j < hi) tmp[k++] = a[j++];\n        for (int x = lo; x < hi; x++) a[x] = tmp[x];\n        return c;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        long[] tmp = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        System.out.println(sortCount(a, tmp, 0, n));\n    }\n}\n"
  },
